From 72eecbe900fb7acebb985efdaf582e0229139bc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Palinar <marco@street63.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 03:56:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Pipeline streamed DiT blocks and add an FP16 GEMM path
 (H3_FP16_GEMM)

Two changes to the streamed-weights denoise, measured on the production
workload (640x832, first+last conditioned, 4 steps, RX 6900 XT eGPU):
22f roll 765 s -> 317 s, 39f roll 1051 s -> 391 s, denoise at 39f
~823 s -> 156 s. Both preserve every quality gate (details below).

1. Pipelined block boundaries (bit-identical; the 608x352/22f fox
   reference md5 886b40d1... is unchanged). h3_gpu_submit at every block
   boundary waited on everything in flight, so the GPU idled through
   each block's CPU-side MPSGraph encode. h3_gpu_submit_boundary commits
   without draining and returns a fence for the committed buffer; the
   streaming slots grow from two to three, and each slot holds the fence
   of its last consumer, waited by the prefetch thread before its DMA
   overwrites the slot (in steady state the guarded block is two
   boundaries old and the wait returns immediately).

2. Opt-in FP16 GEMM path for the streamed block weights (H3_FP16_GEMM=1).
   MPSGraph's BF16 matmul with an in-graph transpose runs at 2.0 TFLOP/s
   on gfx1030; the same shapes in FP16 run at 26.5 (src/gemm_probe.m in
   the revontuli repo). Weights are rewritten as IEEE FP16 in VRAM after
   each block upload (h3_bf16_to_f16_inplace -- exact within FP16 range,
   BF16 has fewer mantissa bits; saturations to +-HALF_MAX are counted
   and reported under H3_PROFILE). qkv/out/fc1 then run through an FP16
   matmul with power-of-two range guards: weights and activations scale
   by 2^-3 into the cast, the output rescales by 2^6 after casting back
   to BF16 -- exponent-only, zero mantissa cost.

   fc2 is the exception, found by bisection (H3_FP16_SKIP): its input is
   the SwiGLU output, which carries activation outliers past FP16 range
   even scaled -- qkv+out+fc1 in FP16 is healthy, adding fc2 collapses
   the video to black (inf -> NaN through the residual). fc2 stays BF16
   in memory and runs on h3_gpu_linear_bf16_f32compute: both operands
   cast up in-graph, FP32 matmul (19.7 TFLOP/s measured), cast back. The
   FP16 path also forces the separate fc1/SwiGLU/fc2 MLP, because the
   fused BF16 MLP graph reads fc1/fc2 as BF16 placeholders and cannot
   see the in-place rewrite.

   Verified on the game workload: YAVG 131.2 vs 131.6 reference,
   PSNR 39.5 dB / SSIM 0.992 against the BF16 output on a pinned seed,
   zero saturations, and TacticaArena's own gates pass at 39f
   (identitydecay first-vs-last IoU 0.9625 vs the 0.9426 the shipped
   baseline recorded; bodyplan drift 0.0167 against tol 0.12). The SDPA
   int32-overflow head-split engages at these shapes and the output is
   clean through it.

Also: H3_SDPA_SPLIT_THRESHOLD lowers the SDPA split gate (VRAM-pressure
lever, default unchanged and verified), and H3_DEBUG_GPU_GAPS prints the
union of command-buffer GPU spans per profile phase against their wall
window, so GPU idle bubbles are measurable instead of inferred.

